      "additions": 12,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/blob/8043d830423e46bdb096a166929a1fbd5aa36b63/torchtitan%2Fexperiments%2Fgraph_trainer%2Fautoresearch%2Fauto_fuser.md",
      "changes": 12,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/torchtitan/contents/torchtitan%2Fexperiments%2Fgraph_trainer%2Fautoresearch%2Fauto_fuser.md?ref=8043d830423e46bdb096a166929a1fbd5aa36b63",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "torchtitan/experiments/graph_trainer/autoresearch/auto_fuser.md",
      "patch": "@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@\n+---\n+name: auto-fuser\n+description: Optimize GraphTrainer regions through kernel fusion with parallel implementation agents, preserving bitwise and memory parity while targeting the local GPU roofline.\n+---\n+\n+# Auto Fuser\n+\n+You're responsible for reaching the roofline local kernel performance while preserving bitiwse parithy and memory parity with the original model through kernel fusions.\n+\n+You can assume gemms, attention and communication kernels have been well optimized. So they form a partitioning boundry that partitions the computation into candidate fusible regions.\n+\n+For each candidate fusible region, you propose fusion plans for this region.For each fusion plan, offload the kernel implementation to parallel sub-agents. The same criteria applies to all kernels: 1. bitwise parity 2. memory parity 3. reach roofline performance (best-effort, bottom line is original implementation).",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/raw/8043d830423e46bdb096a166929a1fbd5aa36b63/torchtitan%2Fexperiments%2Fgraph_trainer%2Fautoresearch%2Fauto_fuser.md",
      "sha": "35b84a06584d6609fdb058db630f17d633c38d54",
      "status": "added"
    }
  ],
